## HQueue Client "NETWORK SERVICE"

**For Windows Client - Scheduled Task (recommended for HQueue Plugin & License Discovery, plus GPU access):**
1. Open Task Scheduler (`taskschd.msc`).
2. Locate the HQueue Client task.
3. Right-click → Properties → General tab.
4. Click "Change User or Group" → enter your Windows username → Check Names → OK.
5. Select "Run only when user is logged on" (keeps the client in your interactive session, critical for GPU access and credential tokens).
6. Click OK (may prompt for your password).
7. Right-click the task → End to stop the current NETWORK SERVICE instance.
8. Make sure you're logged into the render node (via Parsec or local).
9. Right-click → Run to relaunch under your account.

## HQueue ROP Node 
